[center][size=7][b]Not-a-Noble (NaN)[/b][/size]
[size=5][b][color=#FFD700]🌟 OFFICIAL RELEASE (v1.0.0.0) 🌟[/color][/b][/size]
[b][color=#00ff00]STATUS: STABLE[/color][/b][/center]

[center][size=5][b]Important: NaN uses a single-module setup with optional MCM bridge support for easy configuration.[/b][/size]
[size=5][b]Full Turkish (TR) and English (EN) localization is supported.[/b][/size][/center]

[line]

[size=6][b]What Does This Mod Do?[/b][/size]

Not-a-Noble (NaN) completely overhauls the progression system of Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord. Instead of automatically being recognized as a noble just because you gathered some renown, you now start as a mere commoner. To rise through the ranks of Calradia, you must actively earn your titles through wealth, influence, and sheer force. From a lowly Freebooter to a mighty Sovereign, every tier requires specific, immersive milestones.

[line]

[size=6][b]Core Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]The Ascension System:[/b] Progress through distinct nobility tiers: Freebooter ➔ Bannerlord ➔ Chieftain ➔ Count ➔ Duke ➔ Sovereign.
[*][b]Dynamic Milestones:[/b] Earning a title requires more than just clan tier. You will need immense wealth, influence, and even the blood of your enemies.
[*][b]Captive Diplomacy:[/b] A brand new dialogue system! When you capture enemy lords, you can offer them their freedom—[i]if[/i] they formally recognize your new noble title.
[*][b]Persuasion Mini-game:[/b] Captive lords won't bow to a peasant easily. You must persuade them based on your Leadership, Charm, Roguery, and personality traits. Beware: a critical failure will end negotiations immediately!
[*][b]Native Quest Integration:[/b] Track your progress towards your next title directly in the Native Quest Log.
[*][b]Renown Cap Bypass:[/b] Break past the vanilla game's clan tier limitations.
[*][b]Localization:[/b] Full English and Turkish support included.
[/list]

[line]

[size=6][b]The Path to Nobility[/b][/size]

Every tier presents a unique challenge:
[list]
[*][b]Path to a Bannerlord:[/b] Gather enough wealth, renown, and influence to prove you are no longer a simple mercenary.
[*][b]Path to a Chieftain:[/b] Defeat rival lords on the battlefield and force high-ranking captives to acknowledge your legitimacy in exchange for their lives.
[*][b]Path to Higher Titles:[/b] Each subsequent title demands even greater feats of conquest and diplomacy.
[/list]

[line]

[size=6][b]Configuration Modes[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]JSON Mode (Default):[/b] Works without any dependencies. Settings are read from [font=Courier New]config.json[/font].
[*][b]MCM Mode (Optional):[/b] If you have MCM installed, sliders appear automatically within the same [font=Courier New]Not-a-Noble[/font] module. No separate downloads required.
[/list]

Configurable settings include: Requirement thresholds for every single tier (Gold, Influence, Captures, Releases), Persuasion difficulty caps, and more.

[line]

[size=6][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download the latest package and extract it to your Bannerlord [font=Courier New]Modules[/font] folder.
[*]Enable [font=Courier New]NaN[/font] in the launcher.
[*][b]Load Order:[/b] Place NaN after official modules and framework mods.
[/list]

[line]

[size=6][b]FAQ[/b][/size]

[b]Q: How do I force a lord to recognize my title?[/b]
A: Defeat them in battle, take them as a prisoner in your main party, and speak to them. A new dialogue option will appear allowing you to negotiate their release.

[b]Q: Why did the lord refuse my offer immediately?[/b]
A: Lords are proud. If your relationship with them is too low (below 7), they will refuse to even entertain the thought of calling you a noble.

[b]Q: Do I need MCM?[/b]
A: No, it's optional. The mod works fine with default settings or manual JSON edits.

[b]Q: Is it safe to add mid-save?[/b]
A: Yes. It is perfectly safe to add to an existing campaign.

[line]

